name duel-offset-1
timeout 600

# THE ASYMMETRIC DUEL, GEOMETRY 2 OF 8: OFFSET. Same two jets and the same loadout as
# duel-headon.fbm; the two briefed vectors cross at 50 deg instead of 180, so neither jet is on the
# other's nose and the whole engagement is flown off the wing line.
#
# WHY THE ASPECT IS A VARIABLE AND NOT A DECORATION: a launch zone is an integration from the
# launcher's own velocity against the target's (weapons/FBLaunchZone). At 180 deg of aspect the whole
# closure counts for the round; on a 50 deg crossing a large part of it is CROSS-range, Rtr collapses
# and both trigger gates move inwards. The two weapons do not move by the same amount, which is the
# point of running the geometry at all.
#
# THE SECOND EFFECT IS ONE-SIDED AND IT IS THE REASON THIS GEOMETRY IS IN THE CAMPAIGN. The N019's
# search pattern is 30 deg of azimuth either side of a DISCRETE zone switch (sensors.md §4.9), against
# the APG-68's 60. A target 25 deg off the nose sits inside both; a target that then drifts outward
# leaves the MiG's window first. And the N019's Doppler rejection is quantified and range-dependent
# (81 kt beyond 8 nm) where the APG-68's is generic — a crossing target has less radial velocity, so
# this is also the geometry that asks whether the MiG can HOLD what it finds.
#
# THE MiG IS VECTORED, because that is what this aircraft is for: one GCI call at t=20 puts the scan
# elevation and the ZONE where the controller says the bandit is. Without it the crossing puts the
# F-16 outside the 30 deg window and the run measures a mis-vectored MiG rather than a geometry
# (measured, first cut: eng_detect_s = -1 over the whole 600 s).
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 (TIMEOUT), both alive, and the two sides fail for OPPOSITE reasons. MEASURED:
# the F-16 detects at t=24.0 and shoots twice (t=171.8 at 9.63 nm, Rtr 9.79); both rounds run out of
# flight time 25.5 m and 19.4 m out, because a crossing target spends the round's energy on turning.
# The MiG detects at t=117.2 (25.4 nm, azimuth +36.5 in the ZONE the controller put it in) and NEVER
# LOCKS: its track drops three times, each with `coastS=9` on a 3.0 s frame — one look, then the +-6 deg
# elevation bar loses a target whose depression is walking outwards, and the 6 s inertial-tracking
# limit runs out before the next frame reaches it. It goes defensive at t=191.4 and stays there for
# 407.6 s without ever having a firing solution. The crossing geometry therefore costs the F-16 its
# terminal accuracy and the MiG its track file; on a 50 deg crossing neither weapon system delivers.

unit viper
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.40000 8000 115.0 450     # 25 deg south of the line to the MiG
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set store 8 aim9
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 46.42000 7.60000 8000 450
  objective kill unit fulcrum
  objective survive

unit fulcrum
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 46.90000 7.85000 8000 245.0 450     # 25 deg south of the line to the F-16: tracks cross at 50
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set brief_gci 20 270 111 8                # "bandit bearing 270 for 111, angels 8": elevation + ZONE
  set task intercept
  wp 46.51000 6.75000 8000 450
  objective kill unit viper
  objective survive
